1.bug_scenario:
In a JSX-returning function, using a logical “&&” expression with extra parentheses around the JSX fragment causes the new indent rule (4.1.0) to miscompute indentation. In the example:

    function A() {
        return (
            <div>
                {
                    b && (
                        <div>
                        </div>
                    )
                }
            </div>
        );
    }

ESLint reports “Expected 16 spaces but found 20” on the inner `<div>` even though the code was considered correctly indented in ESLint 4.0.  Removing the parentheses or changing the expression form makes the indentation pass again.
